From 1c38cc681b42c2f8f74464d63dde510f7ea2221f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:15:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ccci: quiesce CCIF and preserve modem stop failures

A completed stop must distinguish platform power-off failure from GATED.
Preserve negative PM errors and require logical runtime suspension before
continuing the existing power-off sequence. Keep a terminal failed-stop
state and reject later FSM commands instead of reporting stopped and
allowing another start after an uncertain power transition.

Prepare CCIF in process context before platform power-off: retain an
independent DATA0 IRQ mask while draining the empty-interrupt poller,
synchronize DATA1, and drain SRAM/status work and in-flight TX sections.
Keep reset and clock-off in the successful GATED completion path. Preserve
the guarded register-access wrappers and the IRQ-safe watchdog callback.

Track queued STOP completion so GET_MD_STATE reports EINPROGRESS until
callbacks finish, then return any latched stop errno. This supports an
owner waiting for completed stop rather than asynchronous acceptance or
an ambiguous public state. Module unload and manual unbind remain disabled;
DPMAIF stop-error handling and full transport teardown are separate work.

Exercise production start/stop/IRQ/poll/TX and PM/FSM functions, including
concurrent mask retirement, waiter errors and pending-command completion.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/MTK_kernel_device_modules/blob/3c4ccd07d5624879555ec710c11bb8818e5cb5c6/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.c
Link: https://docs.kernel.org/core-api/genericirq.html
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
 drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/fsm/ccci_fsm.c    |  64 +-
 .../mediatek/eccci/fsm/ccci_fsm_internal.h    |   5 +-
 .../misc/mediatek/eccci/fsm/ccci_fsm_ioctl.c  |   7 +
 .../mediatek/eccci/fsm/md_sys1_platform.c     |  11 +-
 drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/fsm/modem_sys1.c  |  17 +-
 drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif.c    |   9 +
 .../misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.c   |  71 ++-
 .../misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_ccif.h   |   2 +-
 drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/inc/ccci_hif.h    |   1 +
 tools/testing/selftests/mtk_ccci/Makefile     |   4 +-
 .../selftests/mtk_ccci/ccif_start_cases.c     | 560 +++++++++++++----
 .../selftests/mtk_ccci/modem_stop_cases.c     | 565 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../selftests/mtk_ccci/test_ccif_start.py     |  56 +-
 .../selftests/mtk_ccci/test_modem_stop.py     |  76 +++
